          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most basements, the Frigidaire 50-pint on a hose to a floor drain is all you need: Energy Star efficient, easy to live with and big enough for most basements under roughly 1,500 square feet. Choose the GE pump model if the drain is uphill, and the Midea Cube if you are stuck with a bucket, since its tank stretches the time between trips. If the basement is large, cold or chronically damp, pass on the portables and go straight to the Aprilaire E080 or a Santa Fe unit.
          </p>
